+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+## Intent for the next leg
+
+The external Cypress acceptance suite reports five real product defects that the
+in-harness happy-dom suite cannot reproduce, because happy-dom re-queries the
+DOM after each step while a real browser holds element references across an
+interaction. Both root causes are browser-only, so they are pinned here as
+source-level conformance checks (matching the project's existing
+`@captain @conformance` skeleton convention), not as behavioural scenarios.
+
+## Root cause and the two fixes the Crew must make
+
+1. Element identity lost on state change (Cypress failures 1-4: mark all as
+   complete, clear complete state of all, mark item complete, unmark item
+   complete). `js/app.js` `render()` reassigns `list.innerHTML`, discarding and
+   rebuilding every item `<li>` on each toggle. The fix is to mutate the
+   existing item element in place (toggle its `completed` class and checkbox,
+   reflect the mark-all control) instead of rebuilding the list, so the node
+   stays attached across the interaction. The two `item-element-identity`
+   scenarios pin the single-item and mark-all toggle paths.
+
+2. Editing shows the non-edit controls (Cypress failure 5: "should hide other
+   controls when editing"). `index.html` ships no stylesheet, so the
+   `.editing .view { display: none }` rule that hides the checkbox, label and
+   destroy button during editing is absent. The fix is to ship the TodoMVC
+   stylesheet (or an `app.css` override) that hides the non-edit controls while
+   an item carries `editing`. The `editing-hides-controls` scenario pins it.
+
+## Watchbill
+
+`watch1` targets the three conformance scenarios above. They are `@captain`
+skeletons: QM implements the named checks, which redden on the current code and
+green after the Crew fix. Do not remove the `@captain` tag until the check is
+implemented and green.
